- What?


00:26:12.779 --> 00:26:15.281
I'm sorry
for getting you a burger.


00:26:15.315 --> 00:26:17.795
- Why are you sorry for...
- Well, I should have
gotten you hay.


00:26:42.076 --> 00:26:43.778
Hey.


00:26:43.810 --> 00:26:45.913
Hey, what's going on?


00:26:45.945 --> 00:26:47.114
Come here.


00:26:47.146 --> 00:26:50.284
This thing...
he follows me.


00:26:50.317 --> 00:26:53.854
- Hey, it's okay.
- I see it
all the time.


00:26:53.886 --> 00:26:54.989
It's gonna be okay.


00:28:54.106 --> 00:28:55.308
I have an appointment.


00:28:56.576 --> 00:28:57.979
Yeah, I know.


00:29:08.087 --> 00:29:09.957
So?


00:29:13.393 --> 00:29:14.436
Okay, so here's the problem.


00:29:14.461 --> 00:29:16.997
Never update
without doing
a manual restart.


00:29:17.029 --> 00:29:18.273
No, that's not true.
He just said,


00:29:18.298 --> 00:29:20.601
"Say yes at the tone,"
and then he died.


00:29:20.634 --> 00:29:23.136
Did you hold down the button
till God shut down
and restarted?


00:29:25.204 --> 00:29:28.174
- No.
- Okay then.


00:29:28.208 --> 00:29:30.411
I see
you pay for the cloud monthly


00:29:30.443 --> 00:29:33.346
so at least you have a backup
of your good deeds and sins.


00:29:35.182 --> 00:29:36.483
Can you see my sins?


00:29:38.285 --> 00:29:39.554
You want me to?


00:29:40.554 --> 00:29:42.856
Okay, so moving on.


00:29:42.890 --> 00:29:44.357
You back up every day, right?


00:29:44.391 --> 00:29:47.060
Yeah, no, no,
I don't, sometimes, maybe.


00:29:47.094 --> 00:29:50.564
Okay, what's going to happen
is we can offer you a discount
on a new system.


00:29:50.596 --> 00:29:52.356
How long have you been
with your current God?


00:29:53.933 --> 00:29:56.135
- Four years.
- Wow.


00:29:56.169 --> 00:29:58.638
Okay, you're supposed
to renew your faith
every 18 months.


00:29:58.672 --> 00:30:00.574
- No, you're not.
- Yeah.


00:30:00.606 --> 00:30:02.247
I'm surprised
he stayed with you
this long.


00:30:06.113 --> 00:30:07.981
Just give me a new model then.


00:30:11.050 --> 00:30:12.452
He'll be shipped to you
by tomorrow.


00:30:12.486 --> 00:30:13.988
How am I gonna pray?


00:30:16.289 --> 00:30:18.925
You'll have to do it manually.


00:30:28.301 --> 00:30:30.003
God...


00:30:35.208 --> 00:30:37.644
are you there?


00:30:42.249 --> 00:30:43.483
Hello?


00:30:47.421 --> 00:30:49.289
God?


00:30:49.323 --> 00:30:51.259
This is so stupid.


00:30:56.963 --> 00:30:58.965
Where are your parents?


00:31:09.175 --> 00:31:11.511
God... Shit.


00:31:12.746 --> 00:31:14.615
God 2.0 customer service.


00:31:14.647 --> 00:31:16.416
This phone call may be recorded.


00:31:16.450 --> 00:31:18.117
So, I've been
trying to pray manually


00:31:18.151 --> 00:31:21.288
and, nobody's answering.


00:31:21.320 --> 00:31:25.392
So, I feel... kind of stupid,


00:31:25.424 --> 00:31:30.163
and I was just wondering
if maybe...


00:31:30.196 --> 00:31:35.635
you could talk back to me
while I do it?


00:31:35.669 --> 00:31:38.172
Ma'am, we do not provide
spiritual responses


00:31:38.204 --> 00:31:40.406
to God 2.0 customers
over the phone.


00:31:40.440 --> 00:31:43.210
I can sign you up
for an automated
hotline service


00:31:43.242 --> 00:31:45.511
for just a $199 per mont.


00:31:45.545 --> 00:31:49.249
No, no, of course you don't.


00:31:49.281 --> 00:31:50.660
That's... Just...
I actually was asking


00:31:50.683 --> 00:31:52.494
just if you could
maybe do just quick response,


00:31:52.519 --> 00:31:54.421
like, um,
just an inspirational quote,


00:31:54.453 --> 00:31:58.625
you know, "Best preparation
for tomorrow is..."


00:31:58.657 --> 00:32:02.096
Or something about today
or just getting through.


00:32:02.128 --> 00:32:03.596
N.


00:32:06.298 --> 00:32:07.634
I'm sorry, ma'a.


00:32:07.666 --> 00:32:09.670
Is there anything else
I can help you with?


00:32:11.570 --> 00:32:13.707
Hell?


00:32:13.740 --> 00:32:15.710
Hello, ma'a?


00:33:07.794 --> 00:33:09.430
Buenos días, Larry.


00:33:09.462 --> 00:33:12.699
- God.
- ¿Inglés?


00:33:12.731 --> 00:33:16.135
- Sí, sí, inglés.
- Good morning, Larry!


00:33:16.169 --> 00:33:19.740
Congratulations
for choosing God 2.0!
New and improved!


00:33:19.772 --> 00:33:22.843
Wireless, waterproof,
non-flammable
and simply indestructible.


00:33:22.875 --> 00:33:24.744
Made exclusively
from recycled bots,


00:33:24.778 --> 00:33:28.082
God 2.0 is saving you
and the planet.


00:33:28.115 --> 00:33:30.250
Larry, come on down
to Mattress Deluxe


00:33:30.282 --> 00:33:33.119
where we have
thousands of mattresses
at wholesale prices!


00:33:33.153 --> 00:33:35.288
Jesus fucking Christ.


00:33:35.322 --> 00:33:38.791
You used the Lord's
name in vain.
One sin recorded.


00:33:38.825 --> 00:33:40.827
You having trouble
gaining muscle mass?


00:33:40.861 --> 00:33:42.262
- No.
- Of course you do!


00:33:42.296 --> 00:33:45.132
Trainers are going
out of business
because of protein water.


00:33:45.164 --> 00:33:47.800
Make it stop.
Stop ads, please.


00:33:47.834 --> 00:33:51.337
To stop advertisements,
sign up for Premium God 2.0.


00:33:51.371 --> 00:33:54.875
To roll your eyes at God
is a sign of contempt.


00:33:54.907 --> 00:33:56.309
One sin recorded.


00:33:56.343 --> 00:33:59.480
- Can you see me?
- Yes, I see everything.


00:33:59.512 --> 00:34:02.516
The new God 2.0 is equipped
with visual sensor technology.


00:34:04.351 --> 00:34:07.855
- Shit.
- Swearing.
One sin recorded.


00:34:07.887 --> 00:34:10.224
Turn off.


00:34:10.257 --> 00:34:13.260
The new God 2.0
has an eternal battery life,


00:34:13.293 --> 00:34:15.362
and cannot be powered down.


00:34:15.394 --> 00:34:17.130
Forever in your presence.


00:34:17.164 --> 00:34:21.335
Making you
a better person, always.


00:34:24.938 --> 00:34:27.907
No, no, no, no, no!


00:34:57.570 --> 00:34:59.931
You know, I haven't
been back to this area
since I was a kid.


00:35:02.342 --> 00:35:03.876
There was a slight incident.


00:35:03.909 --> 00:35:08.148
There was some fireworks
and a friend's robot.


00:35:09.815 --> 00:35:10.918
What happened?


00:35:14.853 --> 00:35:16.590
I might have blown it up.


00:35:19.960 --> 00:35:21.661
And I was never invited back,
you know,


00:35:21.695 --> 00:35:22.963
so I'm feeling the pressure.


00:35:22.996 --> 00:35:25.498
Okay, probably best
not to mention that
at dinner tonight.


00:35:25.532 --> 00:35:26.809
No, you don't think
they'd like that?


00:35:26.833 --> 00:35:28.635
- Probably not.
- Probably not.


00:35:28.668 --> 00:35:30.445
I thought it'd make me
a bit dangerous,
but whatever.


00:35:30.469 --> 00:35:33.407
I get it. I get it.


00:35:33.440 --> 00:35:36.376
But I'm serious,
I'm really nervous.


00:35:36.409 --> 00:35:40.313
You know, I've never been
with someone of your kind.


00:35:40.347 --> 00:35:42.815
What, someone so privileged,
and so self-loathing?


00:35:42.849 --> 00:35:45.485
Yeah, all my favorite parts
about you.


00:35:45.518 --> 00:35:47.487
I was actually
having some doubts


00:35:47.519 --> 00:35:50.324
- about you and I.
- Hey! That's mean.


00:35:50.356 --> 00:35:52.425
I think it's a little odd


00:35:52.458 --> 00:35:55.862
that you would use
my childhood sippy cup
as an ashtray.


00:35:55.894 --> 00:35:58.431
You... The childhood
sippy cup is odd.


00:35:58.465 --> 00:36:00.400
- Who gave you the sippy cup?
- My mom.


00:36:00.432 --> 00:36:02.969
It's exactly for that reason


00:36:03.003 --> 00:36:05.606
I find the sippy cup
a little bit weird.


00:36:05.639 --> 00:36:08.507
- It's sentimental.
- Do you not think
that that's a reminder


00:36:08.541 --> 00:36:12.646
of what it was like
to attach to the last...


00:36:12.679 --> 00:36:17.583
I'm going to say it,
nipple-like thing
in your life?


00:36:20.753 --> 00:36:22.456
No, seriously.
Seriously.


00:36:22.489 --> 00:36:24.592
Is she... is she going
to hate me?


00:36:25.858 --> 00:36:26.858
Yeah.


00:36:28.795 --> 00:36:30.731
Really?


00:36:30.764 --> 00:36:32.967
- Is she really mean?
- Yeah.


00:36:34.333 --> 00:36:36.436
Well, I'm really great.


00:36:36.469 --> 00:36:38.605
So I'm going
to make this amazing.


00:36:38.637 --> 00:36:39.998
She's going to love me.
Watch this.


00:36:41.340 --> 00:36:45.012
So strange.
What a strange... house


00:36:45.045 --> 00:36:47.614
Is that... is that...


00:36:47.646 --> 00:36:49.349
Do you have a dog?
Is that...?


00:36:49.382 --> 00:36:51.918
- No.
- Do you think that's something on my shoe?


00:36:51.951 --> 00:36:55.289
- Look... Do you think
that's dog poo?
- No, you look fine.


00:36:55.322 --> 00:36:58.659
I cannot go into your house
smelling like dog shit.


00:36:58.692 --> 00:37:01.961
- Yeah.
- That's just a no-go.


00:37:01.994 --> 00:37:04.297
This is so embarrassing.
Are you sure?


00:37:04.331 --> 00:37:06.400
- Yeah, you're fine.
- I smell like poo.


00:37:06.432 --> 00:37:08.568
Ooh! The door opened.


00:37:08.601 --> 00:37:10.436
- Where's your mom?
- Hello, darling!


00:37:10.469 --> 00:37:11.672
Come on in.


00:37:11.704 --> 00:37:14.307
Your father and sister
are in the game room.


00:37:14.340 --> 00:37:15.608
God.


00:37:22.782 --> 00:37:26.385
- If you wanna watch the master.
- That's what I rolled.


00:37:26.418 --> 00:37:27.987
See how it goes.


00:37:28.021 --> 00:37:31.358
Take a nap, he takes forever.


00:37:31.391 --> 00:37:32.626
Yeah, thank you.


00:37:34.360 --> 00:37:35.429
Watch, guys. Watch, guys.


00:37:36.762 --> 00:37:38.398
- Yeah!
- No!


00:37:38.431 --> 00:37:39.766
I'm so pumped.


00:37:39.798 --> 00:37:41.702
- Wow.
- So gonna pl...
I'm killing on this.


00:37:41.735 --> 00:37:43.737
Looks like you built
a water park instead, Dad.


00:37:43.769 --> 00:37:45.505
Don't tell your mother.


00:37:45.538 --> 00:37:47.974
Ron, I think that's enough now.


00:37:48.007 --> 00:37:50.510
We should never
have installed
a home optics system.


00:37:50.543 --> 00:37:53.512
Word of advice.
Keep the home optic stuff
to the bedroom,


00:37:53.545 --> 00:37:55.724
- you don't need it
for the whole house.
- Eww, Dad. Stop.


00:37:55.748 --> 00:37:58.385
No, most accidents
happen in the bedroom.


00:37:58.418 --> 00:38:01.387
So, you finally admit
that Olivia is an accident?


00:38:01.420 --> 00:38:03.456
You're an accident, Liam.


00:38:03.489 --> 00:38:05.010
Except you happened
in the living room.


00:38:06.126 --> 00:38:08.561
- Wait, where?
- Ay, ay, ay.


00:38:08.594 --> 00:38:09.797
Right, your go.


00:38:10.829 --> 00:38:12.532
No cheating like your sister.


00:38:13.867 --> 00:38:15.402
- Yes!
- Watch and weep.


00:38:16.536 --> 00:38:20.673
Well, apparently
mission control
lost contact with him.


00:38:20.706 --> 00:38:23.876
You'd think they'd just
get robots to do it by now.


00:38:23.909 --> 00:38:25.911
Why would anybody go up there?


00:38:25.945 --> 00:38:29.083
Sometimes you
just need some space.


00:38:30.550 --> 00:38:32.652
I'm so sorry.
I'm so sorry.


00:38:32.684 --> 00:38:36.422
Nina, let him do it.
That's what he's
programmed for.


00:38:36.456 --> 00:38:38.056
We just adopted him
a couple of days ago.


00:38:39.192 --> 00:38:42.596
We only rescue.
It's the best thing to do.


00:38:42.628 --> 00:38:43.972
Why don't they rescue
the space guy?


00:38:43.996 --> 00:38:46.967
The news said
that rescue mission
is impossible.


00:38:47.000 --> 00:38:49.702
I wonder
what he's thinking about.


00:38:49.735 --> 00:38:52.405
Floating up there,
all by himself.


00:38:53.873 --> 00:38:56.976
Probably... nothing.


00:38:57.010 --> 00:38:58.677
I think that that's
the best part,


00:38:58.710 --> 00:39:00.813
you can just shut off
the old computer.


00:39:00.847 --> 00:39:02.916
So you wouldn't be
thinking about me then, Ron?


00:39:02.949 --> 00:39:04.717
Well, of course, hon.


00:39:04.751 --> 00:39:09.121
By "nothing", I meant
nothing else but you.


00:39:09.155 --> 00:39:10.556
- Good save.
- Thanks.


00:39:10.590 --> 00:39:11.925
No, I'm not buying it, Liam.


00:39:11.958 --> 00:39:14.460
I can't even
float alone through space


00:39:14.494 --> 00:39:15.829
without her telling me
what to do.


00:39:17.931 --> 00:39:19.498
You know, I think there's,


00:39:19.532 --> 00:39:22.202
something poetic about floating
through space like that.


00:39:22.235 --> 00:39:23.737
Why?


00:39:23.769 --> 00:39:26.039
Well, 'cause you know
how it's gonna end.


00:39:26.072 --> 00:39:27.940
What's poetic about dying?


00:39:30.476 --> 00:39:31.710
Everything.


00:39:31.744 --> 00:39:33.847
It's so primitive to think


00:39:33.880 --> 00:39:35.681
that the only way
a life has meaning


00:39:35.715 --> 00:39:37.684
is if you know
it's going to end.


00:39:37.717 --> 00:39:39.652
Um, not really, Mom.


00:39:39.686 --> 00:39:42.588
I mean, not everyone
is blessed with
the luxury of eternal life.


00:39:42.621 --> 00:39:44.224
I'm sorry.


00:39:44.257 --> 00:39:47.760
Should we be ashamed
of how blessed we are?


00:39:47.793 --> 00:39:49.496
No, I just don't think


00:39:49.528 --> 00:39:51.168
that we should rub it in
our guest's face.


00:39:53.766 --> 00:39:55.068
I apologize, Nina.


00:39:55.101 --> 00:39:57.771
I didn't mean to make you
feel uncomfortable.


00:39:57.804 --> 00:40:00.139
Don't worry, I'm...


00:40:00.172 --> 00:40:02.876
I'm not uncomfortable at all.


00:40:02.909 --> 00:40:04.543
I actually like being mortal.


00:40:04.577 --> 00:40:07.146
See, not everyone
is dying not to die.


00:40:07.179 --> 00:40:10.684
Sure. But I would assume
that given the choice,


00:40:10.717 --> 00:40:13.719
anyone with a sane mind
would choose to go on living.


00:40:13.753 --> 00:40:15.588
Well, I didn't have a choice.


00:40:17.690 --> 00:40:20.860
I wasn't born
in the same tier group
you were,


00:40:20.893 --> 00:40:22.862
so I didn't get to choose.


00:40:23.929 --> 00:40:25.532
But I'm okay with that.


00:40:27.166 --> 00:40:30.070
But don't you feel like
you're missing out
on so much time?


00:40:30.103 --> 00:40:33.706
Well, I mean, time
just becomes more precious.


00:40:36.175 --> 00:40:38.777
There we go
with the primitive thinking.


00:40:38.811 --> 00:40:41.114
What's your issue?


00:40:41.146 --> 00:40:43.083
We, as a family,


00:40:43.115 --> 00:40:45.150
of course we're
really excited about Nina.


00:40:45.184 --> 00:40:48.688
She's really lovely.


00:40:48.721 --> 00:40:52.192
- But, we do have some...
- Concerns.


00:40:52.224 --> 00:40:56.795
- Concerns, yes.
- We have some concerns.


00:40:56.829 --> 00:40:59.032
All right, I mean,
I'd love to hear them.


00:41:05.204 --> 00:41:07.306
None? Nothing?


00:41:07.340 --> 00:41:10.643
Mom and Dad think
you dating a mortal
is a waste of time.


00:41:10.677 --> 00:41:13.012
I never said it in those words.


00:41:13.045 --> 00:41:15.648
Look, Nina, I-I think
you're very lovely.


00:41:15.681 --> 00:41:19.318
But we have to be
realistic here.


00:41:19.351 --> 00:41:21.788
Well, I mean,


00:41:21.820 --> 00:41:25.157
please, do tell us
your ultra-modern take
on this...


00:41:27.059 --> 00:41:28.695
It's a big sacrifice


00:41:28.728 --> 00:41:31.797
to waste time on something
that's going to end.


00:41:31.831 --> 00:41:36.135
And especially when that end
is so heartbreaking.


00:41:36.168 --> 00:41:37.737
No offense, Nina.


00:41:37.769 --> 00:41:39.606
None taken.


00:41:39.639 --> 00:41:42.876
She's going to get sick,
and then she will die.


00:41:42.909 --> 00:41:45.811
Do you really need to be
around there for that, Liam?


00:41:47.213 --> 00:41:48.648
Yeah.


00:41:48.681 --> 00:41:50.016
I love this woman,


00:41:50.048 --> 00:41:52.853
so I want to spend
all the time I can with her.


00:41:54.219 --> 00:41:56.188
Don't you see
what you're doing, Nina?


00:41:56.222 --> 00:41:58.190
- Hold on.
- I'm not doing anything.


00:41:58.224 --> 00:42:00.827
You're dragging him
down with you.


00:42:00.860 --> 00:42:03.096
Why can't you find someone
of your own kind?


00:42:03.128 --> 00:42:05.231
You know...


00:42:06.065 --> 00:42:09.369
I wasn't planning
on telling you guys today.


00:42:09.402 --> 00:42:10.704
But...


00:42:13.072 --> 00:42:15.942
I've decided to die naturally
with Nina.


00:42:15.974 --> 00:42:18.744
Excuse me?


00:42:18.777 --> 00:42:19.778
I'm turning it off.


00:42:19.811 --> 00:42:22.916
I don't think so.


00:42:22.949 --> 00:42:26.853
- What?
- I don't wanna live
forever without you.


00:42:26.885 --> 00:42:29.222
That's crazy talk.


00:42:29.255 --> 00:42:31.824
Why, just spend time
with her then.


00:42:31.858 --> 00:42:34.893
- Don't kill yourself over it.
- I'm not killing myself.


00:42:34.927 --> 00:42:37.630
Look, have your fun now,


00:42:37.664 --> 00:42:40.233
and then, when she dies,
do a memory reset.


00:42:40.266 --> 00:42:42.902
Delete her.


00:42:42.934 --> 00:42:44.670
That is so cold.


00:42:44.704 --> 00:42:46.405
I'm a romantic too.


00:42:46.438 --> 00:42:49.376
You've got so much more time
and accomplishments
ahead of you.


00:42:52.344 --> 00:42:55.815
So I can what?
Make more money?


00:42:57.150 --> 00:42:58.684
Then what?
Get another hobby?


00:42:58.717 --> 00:43:00.853
Learn another language
I'm never gonna use?


00:43:00.887 --> 00:43:04.090
When you can do
anything you want tomorrow,


00:43:04.123 --> 00:43:05.826
today doesn't really matter.


00:43:07.927 --> 00:43:09.730
I made my decision.


00:43:12.030 --> 00:43:13.967
You know you can't reverse this.


00:43:14.000 --> 00:43:18.771
Once you switch it off...


00:43:18.804 --> 00:43:21.675
you'll be just like them,
like her.


00:43:24.777 --> 00:43:28.014
You'll age,
you'll get sick
and then...


00:43:28.047 --> 00:43:31.818
Liam, you know, I'd never
ask you to do this for me.


00:43:31.851 --> 00:43:33.186
It's my choice.


00:43:34.387 --> 00:43:36.088
I'm not gonna let this happen.


00:43:36.121 --> 00:43:39.291
Absolutely no way.


00:43:40.092 --> 00:43:43.697
Well, you know,
I think it's about time
I went for a cigarette.


00:43:43.730 --> 00:43:46.065
Great!
She smokes as well!


00:43:46.099 --> 00:43:48.467
As if her life
wasn't short enough.


00:43:48.501 --> 00:43:50.202
